WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.836
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:01.106 --> 00:03.442
[♪ theme song playing]

3
00:03.525 --> 00:04.651
PARK MINJAE'S LIST

4
00:04.735 --> 00:06.028
START DATING...

5
00:36.725 --> 00:41.063
BETWEEN STEPS

6
00:41.688 --> 00:43.940
CHARACTERS, PLACES, ORGANIZATIONS, AND EVENTS IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

7
00:44.024 --> 00:45.651
THIS DRAMA CONTAINS SENSITIVE CONTENT

8
00:51.281 --> 00:53.158
[♪ soft music playing]

9
01:08.465 --> 01:14.971
[singing] ♪ Carrying a fragrance not too strong ♪

10
01:17.307 --> 01:22.187
♪ You sit demurely on the dark brown table ♪

11
01:22.270 --> 01:23.271
[grunts]

12
01:25.399 --> 01:30.529
♪ It feels awkward to even speak to you ♪

13
01:39.621 --> 01:45.127
[continues singing indistinctly] ♪ Because you sit there ever so quietly ♪

14
01:45.836 --> 01:47.379
[keys jingling]

15
01:48.213 --> 01:50.173
[gate opens]

16
01:55.178 --> 01:56.179
[gate closes]

17
01:59.641 --> 02:01.143
[digital beep from door]

18
02:01.226 --> 02:02.227
EPISODE 3

19
02:02.310 --> 02:03.854
[TV playing]

20
02:03.937 --> 02:04.938
You're late.

21
02:05.730 --> 02:09.276
Yeah, I haven't seen these friends in a while, and I lost track of time.

22
02:09.359 --> 02:10.944
You didn't drink much, did you?

23
02:11.027 --> 02:14.281
No, not much. Just a little with dinner.

24
02:15.782 --> 02:16.992
Don't lock the door yet.

25
02:17.576 --> 02:18.994
Youjin is not home.

26
02:20.620 --> 02:22.330
She's still not home at this hour?

27
02:24.082 --> 02:26.543
The other grad students threw her a welcome party.

28
02:27.210 --> 02:28.211
Oh.

29
02:29.671 --> 02:30.881
[Miyoung grunts]

30
02:43.059 --> 02:44.144
Jeez, you scared me.

31
02:44.728 --> 02:46.062
What are you doing?

32
02:46.646 --> 02:48.356
-Honey. -Let go.

33
02:48.440 --> 02:53.028
So I was on my way home just now, and you know that alley next to our place?

34
02:53.528 --> 02:56.031
There's a streetlight there, right?

35
02:56.114 --> 02:57.115
A streetlight?

36
02:57.616 --> 02:58.742
Yeah.

37
02:58.825 --> 03:03.830
There were these two young people there, holding each other and kissing.

38
03:04.956 --> 03:07.000
-In the alley right next to our place? -Yeah.

39
03:07.083 --> 03:08.543
Oh my. Who were they?

40
03:08.627 --> 03:10.545
Do you know them? Do they live around here?

41
03:11.505 --> 03:14.299
I don't know. I've never seen them before.

42
03:15.342 --> 03:20.514
But seeing them reminded me of us back when we were dating, you know?

43
03:20.597 --> 03:21.598
What?

44
03:23.266 --> 03:26.061
How about a kiss? It's been a while.

45
03:26.144 --> 03:28.813
Stop it. What's gotten into you?

46
03:28.897 --> 03:30.565
Come on. Just one kiss.

47
03:30.649 --> 03:32.692
God, stop it.

48
03:33.318 --> 03:36.071
Miyoung, come on. Just give me one kiss.

49
03:36.154 --> 03:38.907
Come on, I said no. Stop it!

50
03:38.990 --> 03:40.659
Please, just one kiss.

51
03:40.742 --> 03:43.328
Stop it. Gosh, stop. [giggling]

52
03:43.411 --> 03:45.622
Jeez, will you guys stop already?

53
03:47.040 --> 03:48.208
Dad, are you drunk?

54
03:49.459 --> 03:53.046
If you're drunk, just go to bed. Stop bothering Mom and leave her alone.

55
03:53.672 --> 03:55.131
Come on, go to bed already.

56
03:55.215 --> 03:57.217
-[digital beep from door] -What are you doing? Come on.

57
03:57.300 --> 03:59.386
-[Youjin] I'm home. -[door closes]

58
04:01.304 --> 04:02.806
You need to come home earlier.

59
04:02.889 --> 04:03.890
-Hey! -[Youjin] Okay.

60
04:03.974 --> 04:05.892
Do you know what time it is?

61
04:06.434 --> 04:08.728
You need to start coming home earlier, young lady.

62
04:08.812 --> 04:11.147
Look at the time! You've been drinking, haven't you?

63
04:11.648 --> 04:14.442
Hey. Don't call your sister "young lady," okay?

64
04:14.526 --> 04:16.611
And what do you mean, your dad is bothering me?

65
04:16.695 --> 04:20.282
You're the one who bothers me the most, you know? It's you. God!

66
04:31.668 --> 04:33.670
[♪ pleasant piano music playing]

67
05:03.450 --> 05:05.201
[grunts softly]

68
05:12.626 --> 05:13.877
I don't know.

69
05:18.673 --> 05:19.674
[grunts]

70
05:25.221 --> 05:27.223
[♪ music continues]

71
06:10.183 --> 06:13.395
SLAM DUNK

72
06:59.399 --> 07:03.737
SEOHAN NATIONAL UNIVERSITY TEST PAPER NAME LIM YOUJIN

73
07:09.075 --> 07:11.202
TEST PAPER NAME KIM SEJIN

74
07:12.787 --> 07:14.789
-[door opens] -[♪ music ends]

75
07:51.910 --> 07:53.995
[Taeho speaking indistinctly]

76
07:59.459 --> 08:01.461
No matter how much you do it, we...

77
08:01.544 --> 08:03.797
-You're already here. -Hello.

78
08:03.880 --> 08:06.090
Youjin, you're here early.

79
08:06.174 --> 08:07.717
She got here earlier than we did.

80
08:07.801 --> 08:09.719
[Youjin] I can't be late on the first day.

81
08:10.345 --> 08:13.223
You never disappoint, Youjin. That's why I got you a coffee.

82
08:13.306 --> 08:15.308
Thank you. I appreciate it.

83
08:18.978 --> 08:20.063
Who are you?

84
08:25.902 --> 08:26.903
[phone vibrating]

85
08:28.655 --> 08:30.240
[Taeho] Minjae, where are you?

86
08:31.241 --> 08:33.868
[Minjae] On the bus. I'll be there in five.

87
08:40.375 --> 08:42.585
Did Youjin come?

88
08:49.926 --> 08:51.177
What about Lim Youjin?

89
08:58.393 --> 09:00.061
Did our new lab mate Youjin...

90
09:02.480 --> 09:04.649
[inhales sharply, sighs]

91
09:07.152 --> 09:09.654
Morning. Morning.

92
09:10.488 --> 09:12.657
[in English] Morning. Good morning.

93
09:13.491 --> 09:14.701
Good morning.

94
09:16.578 --> 09:17.662
[in Korean] Morning.

95
09:17.745 --> 09:20.165
I'm Kim Sejin. Nice to meet you.

96
09:20.874 --> 09:21.875
All right.

97
09:24.711 --> 09:25.712
Okay, sit down.

98
09:26.671 --> 09:30.967
I thought Sejin wouldn't be joining us until the semester started,

99
09:31.050 --> 09:34.095
but he said he could start this month, so I had him come in early.

100
09:35.680 --> 09:39.392
He's new to our school, so help him settle in and look out for him.

101
09:40.018 --> 09:41.019
Oh, okay.

102
09:43.897 --> 09:44.898
Yes.

103
09:45.857 --> 09:49.611
I thought you said there was only one opening in the lab,

104
09:50.945 --> 09:52.155
but there are two of us.

105
09:52.989 --> 09:53.990
Right.

106
09:54.866 --> 10:00.455
We... Our school might be competing in the WRS this year,

107
10:01.748 --> 10:04.626
so the professor told me to take on one more student.

108
10:04.709 --> 10:07.170
[whispering] Hey, what's the WRS?

109
10:07.253 --> 10:09.339
[whispering] It's the World Robot Summit.

110
10:10.298 --> 10:11.299
Yes?

111
10:11.841 --> 10:14.427
But she doesn't even know what the WRS is.

112
10:14.510 --> 10:17.847
Lim Youjin is a student from another department,

113
10:17.931 --> 10:19.599
so she'll still have a lot to learn.

114
10:19.682 --> 10:22.352
So I'd like you to look out for her and help her settle in.

115
10:23.603 --> 10:25.730
-What is it? -Then do we get paid the same?

116
10:26.856 --> 10:28.942
-Yes, you'll get paid the same. -Wait, but--

117
10:29.025 --> 10:33.446
Let's get you two set up with desks first. Let's see. Get up.

118
10:33.529 --> 10:34.530
Then...

119
10:34.989 --> 10:35.990
[grunts]

120
10:41.246 --> 10:42.247
Ah.

121
10:42.330 --> 10:45.333
Youjin, you take this desk. And Sejin, you take this one.

122
10:48.836 --> 10:51.798
But there's no computer at my desk. There's nothing here.

123
10:52.840 --> 10:55.927
I ordered a computer. It should be here soon.

124
10:56.844 --> 10:58.888
So until then...

125
10:58.972 --> 11:02.183
You brought your own laptop, right? Just use that for now.

126
11:02.934 --> 11:04.394
I only brought my tablet.

127
11:05.979 --> 11:07.230
You can use that for now.

128
11:18.283 --> 11:19.284
[Minjae grunts]

129
11:36.175 --> 11:37.802
-Minjae? -Yes.

130
11:37.885 --> 11:40.388
I think this computer is lagging.

131
11:41.723 --> 11:44.475
Right. It's not lagging.

132
11:44.559 --> 11:47.103
That one's just a little slow because it's old.

133
11:48.229 --> 11:49.856
-Yeah. -Okay.

134
11:51.983 --> 11:53.359
[Sejin sighs]

135
12:02.160 --> 12:04.329
So when will my computer get here?

136
12:04.412 --> 12:05.580
Uh...

137
12:05.663 --> 12:07.123
I'm not sure.

138
12:08.207 --> 12:11.002
They said it'd get here soon, so just wait a bit.

139
12:13.004 --> 12:15.214
Then, until mine gets here, how about this?

140
12:16.632 --> 12:21.471
What if we switch desks every day? So we can take turns using the computer?

141
12:22.680 --> 12:26.059
Why should we take turns using my computer? It's mine.

142
12:26.976 --> 12:29.854
How is this yours? It belongs to the lab.

143
12:31.356 --> 12:35.193
That's not what I mean. The lab lead assigned it to me.

144
12:35.276 --> 12:36.736
[Hangyeol] Well...

145
12:38.154 --> 12:41.366
Why don't you play rock-paper-scissors or ghost leg?

146
12:41.449 --> 12:44.035
The winner gets the computer.

147
12:44.118 --> 12:45.536
Yeah, that's a good idea.

148
12:46.120 --> 12:48.414
The winner gets the computer. Fair and square.

149
12:48.498 --> 12:51.834
Come on, there's no need for ghost leg.

150
12:51.918 --> 12:53.419
We have to respect seniority.

151
12:54.003 --> 12:58.257
Youjin joined the lab three days earlier, so she should get it.

152
12:58.341 --> 13:01.594
She has seniority over me just because she joined three days earlier?

153
13:01.677 --> 13:02.678
That's ridiculous.

154
13:04.680 --> 13:09.811
Whether it's three days or three hours, we take seniority seriously in this lab...

155
13:10.895 --> 13:11.938
Mr. Kim.

156
13:15.400 --> 13:17.819
Isn't this mine?

157
13:17.902 --> 13:19.404
It's yours.

158
13:20.905 --> 13:23.699
I mean, even if you had a computer, Youjin,

159
13:23.783 --> 13:26.702
you don't have any actual work to do yet.

160
13:27.495 --> 13:31.791
So you can check your email and look up papers

161
13:31.874 --> 13:33.751
on your, laptop...

162
13:33.835 --> 13:36.212
I mean, that tablet you brought for now.

163
13:36.712 --> 13:38.464
And your computer should be here soon.

164
13:39.048 --> 13:42.969
So just, yeah... Just wait a little bit.

165
13:52.353 --> 13:55.940
[♪ slow string music playing]

166
14:03.614 --> 14:04.866
[phone vibrating]

167
14:10.705 --> 14:13.624
[Minjae] I checked, and it looks like the computer should be here soon.

168
14:13.708 --> 14:15.543
I think you won't have to wait long.

169
14:17.044 --> 14:18.379
[phone vibrating]

170
14:20.923 --> 14:21.924
[Youjin] Okay.

171
14:34.312 --> 14:35.313
[phone vibrating]

172
14:37.899 --> 14:39.275
[Minjae] Do you want some ice cream?

173
14:40.318 --> 14:41.736
What flavor do you like?

174
14:47.867 --> 14:48.868
[phone vibrating]

175
14:50.536 --> 14:52.371
[Youjin] I don't like ice cream.

176
14:53.414 --> 14:55.458
I absolutely hate it. I don't want any.

177
14:56.500 --> 14:58.878
And I will never eat it, ever. It pisses me off.

178
14:58.961 --> 15:00.880
I hate it more than anything in the world.

179
15:06.969 --> 15:08.471
[groans]

180
15:12.475 --> 15:14.352
[Hangyeol] Youjin, over here. No!

181
15:14.435 --> 15:15.436
[Taeho] Block her!

182
15:16.270 --> 15:17.271
Miss!

183
15:17.355 --> 15:18.356
-[grunts] -[Youjin laughs]

184
15:18.439 --> 15:19.440
Nice!

185
15:20.024 --> 15:21.734
-[Sejin sighs] -[chuckles softly]

186
15:21.817 --> 15:25.112
They suck at basketball. They haven't made a single basket.

187
15:27.240 --> 15:28.241
[Chansoo] Hey, now...

188
15:28.324 --> 15:29.325
[Taeho] She can't make it.

189
15:29.742 --> 15:31.452
-[exclaims] -[cheering]

190
15:33.120 --> 15:35.164
She's not even that pretty.

191
15:35.248 --> 15:37.416
What?

192
15:38.709 --> 15:41.879
Let's be honest. She only stands out in an engineering school.

193
15:43.214 --> 15:45.258
There are plenty of pretty girls at Hongik University.

194
15:45.341 --> 15:46.717
She's just average.

195
15:50.846 --> 15:52.473
Have you been to Hongik University?

196
15:55.726 --> 15:57.478
No, I haven't.

197
16:01.148 --> 16:02.149
I have.

198
16:03.317 --> 16:04.318
But...

199
16:06.654 --> 16:07.947
Well, I didn't see any...

200
16:08.531 --> 16:09.532
Let's go.

201
16:10.574 --> 16:11.742
Let's go. [sighs]

202
16:14.453 --> 16:18.332
Hey, you guys are no different. Daejeon is a boring city. Why--

203
16:18.416 --> 16:20.626
That's not true. Daejeon is a super fun city.

204
16:20.710 --> 16:22.837
"Super fun?" Why are you getting all defensive?

205
16:22.920 --> 16:24.630
-[Sejin] No, seriously. -What do you do there?

206
16:24.714 --> 16:25.840
[Sejin] A lot of things.

207
16:27.383 --> 16:29.218
[telephone ringing]

208
16:38.561 --> 16:39.562
Should I take it?

209
16:39.645 --> 16:42.398
Yeah. You can answer all the calls from now on.

210
16:44.108 --> 16:45.109
[Sejin clears throat]

211
16:47.486 --> 16:49.572
This is Professor Ahn's lab.

212
16:50.781 --> 16:51.782
Yes.

213
16:52.742 --> 16:53.743
Yes.

214
16:56.370 --> 16:57.747
All right, got it.

215
17:03.377 --> 17:05.921
Professor Ahn's back from his appointment.

216
17:06.672 --> 17:07.757
Yeah?

217
17:08.257 --> 17:11.218
[Jaehong] You two are the same age and in the same cohort,

218
17:11.302 --> 17:14.138
so just support each other and get along, okay?

219
17:14.722 --> 17:17.350
"Loving your cohort is loving your country."

220
17:17.433 --> 17:19.018
There's a saying like that.

221
17:19.101 --> 17:20.102
Right.

222
17:20.644 --> 17:22.730
[Jaehong] Sejin, did you find a place to stay in Seoul?

223
17:23.606 --> 17:25.483
Yes. I found a place near campus.

224
17:26.067 --> 17:29.028
Actually, it's right by my place.

225
17:29.111 --> 17:31.405
Oh, that's great. So you can help him out then.

226
17:32.657 --> 17:33.658
Sure.

227
17:33.741 --> 17:37.495
Anyway, I'm glad Sejin was able to start early.

228
17:38.496 --> 17:41.332
And I hear KAIST is competing in the WRS this year too?

229
17:41.916 --> 17:45.795
Yes. From what I've heard, Professor Hwang Semin's lab will compete.

230
17:45.878 --> 17:49.048
But their funding from the Ministry of National Defense was cut,

231
17:49.131 --> 17:51.550
so they sat out the last two years.

232
17:51.634 --> 17:53.302
What funding do they have this time?

233
17:53.844 --> 17:54.845
Uh...

234
17:55.846 --> 17:57.890
Not through the Ministry of National Defense.

235
17:57.973 --> 18:00.393
KEIT plans to issue a call for proposals this year.

236
18:00.476 --> 18:02.436
-That's probably why-- -KEIT?

237
18:05.231 --> 18:08.484
But I met Professor Hwang at the seminar two weeks ago,

238
18:09.026 --> 18:10.486
and he didn't mention anything.

239
18:11.946 --> 18:13.823
Well, it's not official yet.

240
18:15.116 --> 18:19.704
But I heard 200 million won has been earmarked for it.

241
18:19.787 --> 18:20.788
200 million?

242
18:20.871 --> 18:22.206
[exclaims softly]

243
18:22.289 --> 18:26.043
Wow. Hwang Semin, that sly fox.

244
18:26.127 --> 18:27.712
-Professor. -Okay, fine.

245
18:28.671 --> 18:32.550
But where did you hear about it? None of us knew about that.

246
18:32.633 --> 18:34.218
I heard it in the restroom.

247
18:35.386 --> 18:36.429
Restroom?

248
18:36.929 --> 18:38.347
While I was relieving myself.

249
18:40.057 --> 18:41.684
Well, I wasn't trying to listen in.

250
18:41.767 --> 18:44.395
I just happened to overhear him talking on the phone.

251
18:44.478 --> 18:47.481
He's pretty sharp.

252
18:48.274 --> 18:49.275
Hmm.

253
18:50.443 --> 18:53.738
Anyway, we need to hurry up and put together our own proposal.

254
18:53.821 --> 18:55.948
Okay, I'll make sure we're well prepared.

255
18:57.158 --> 18:58.826
Right.

256
18:58.909 --> 19:03.080
Didn't KEIT's RFP template change last year?

257
19:03.706 --> 19:05.416
Yes, I'll check.

258
19:05.499 --> 19:07.668
Okay, please look into that first.

259
19:07.752 --> 19:10.296
And keep an eye out. We don't know when it'll be posted.

260
19:10.379 --> 19:11.714
-Okay. -All right.

261
19:11.797 --> 19:13.340
What is KEIT?

262
19:14.008 --> 19:17.178
Korea Planning and Evaluation Institute of Industrial Technology, Ms. Lim.

263
19:17.261 --> 19:18.262
It's an acronym.

264
19:19.805 --> 19:21.474
That little rat...

265
19:22.266 --> 19:23.768
[Chansoo] Why is KEIT doing

266
19:23.851 --> 19:26.020
what the Ministry of National Defense used to do?

267
19:26.604 --> 19:29.857
The civilian sector can be dangerous too, like industrial accident sites.

268
19:29.940 --> 19:31.567
So I guess they'd be interested.

269
19:31.650 --> 19:35.988
So we need to have everything in place to reach around TRL 7 or 8,

270
19:36.071 --> 19:39.784
or at least TRL 5 or 6, to the point where it's ready for application.

271
19:41.786 --> 19:43.996
Both the robot design and the control technology

272
19:44.079 --> 19:45.706
are our proprietary technologies.

273
19:45.790 --> 19:47.917
Make sure to emphasize that all key components,

274
19:48.000 --> 19:50.294
like the actuators and encoders, are made in Korea.

275
19:50.377 --> 19:51.796
-Okay, got it. -Good.

276
19:52.755 --> 19:55.174
We'll need to include the simulation results too.

277
19:55.257 --> 19:58.677
And of course, we'll need visuals to highlight all of that, right?

278
20:00.429 --> 20:03.015
We just need something rough now. We can revise it later.

279
20:03.682 --> 20:07.311
What matters is having a preliminary draft ready by the end of the month.

280
20:07.394 --> 20:08.604
So let's get moving.

281
20:09.563 --> 20:10.564
Okay.

282
20:13.484 --> 20:15.236
-[Chansoo] All right, then. -What about me?

283
20:15.319 --> 20:16.612
What should I do?

284
20:17.738 --> 20:18.864
You?

285
20:20.449 --> 20:21.784
You can...

286
20:22.368 --> 20:23.577
Uh...

287
20:24.620 --> 20:26.205
read some papers.

288
20:26.288 --> 20:27.456
What papers?

289
20:28.916 --> 20:31.293
Anything. Read broadly.

290
20:32.294 --> 20:34.296
You need to get up to speed on current trends

291
20:34.839 --> 20:36.257
What trends?

292
20:37.508 --> 20:39.051
Whatever you find interesting.

293
20:40.970 --> 20:43.222
Read anything that catches your eye. Anything.

294
20:50.062 --> 20:52.064
[♪ pensive music playing]

295
21:26.849 --> 21:29.852
SEOHAN NATIONAL UNIVERSITY

296
21:34.690 --> 21:36.650
Here, I collected all the assignments.

297
21:37.192 --> 21:39.153
You didn't have to carry something so heavy.

298
21:39.236 --> 21:40.446
-Give it to me. -It's okay.

299
21:40.529 --> 21:42.615
-Where should I put it? -You can put it here.

300
21:44.575 --> 21:45.576
[grunts]

301
21:49.830 --> 21:51.957
I'm going to head out now.

302
21:52.541 --> 21:53.751
Huh?

303
21:53.834 --> 21:54.835
Ah!

304
21:54.919 --> 21:56.962
I'm done too, actually. Wait up.

305
21:58.672 --> 21:59.882
Let's head out together.

306
22:05.012 --> 22:06.347
Want to grab dinner together?

307
22:08.098 --> 22:09.600
Do you have any plans tonight?

308
22:11.393 --> 22:13.812
No, I don't.

309
22:15.314 --> 22:17.232
But I'm not hungry at all right now.

310
22:18.233 --> 22:19.234
Oh.

311
22:20.194 --> 22:21.362
[stomach growling]

312
22:27.201 --> 22:29.203
[♪ chill music playing on speakers]

313
22:34.583 --> 22:35.960
So how was your first day?

314
22:37.127 --> 22:39.546
First days are always a little hectic, right?

315
22:41.298 --> 22:43.968
Yeah, I guess.

316
22:47.304 --> 22:51.183
Read as many papers as you can when you have time. It'll help you learn.

317
22:52.810 --> 22:53.811
Okay.

318
22:57.356 --> 22:58.816
You were hungry, weren't you?

319
23:00.901 --> 23:04.071
I'm not eating because I'm hungry. I'm just eating.

320
23:05.572 --> 23:07.241
[muttering] That doesn't fool me.

321
23:08.617 --> 23:09.910
What are you laughing about?

322
23:10.953 --> 23:11.954
I didn't laugh.

323
23:13.747 --> 23:14.957
I don't want to eat anymore.

324
23:15.040 --> 23:16.583
Come on, why?

325
23:17.876 --> 23:19.920
All right, I'm sorry. Eat up. Please.

326
23:30.723 --> 23:31.724
I...

327
23:32.975 --> 23:34.685
don't have a sister.

328
23:36.270 --> 23:39.815
And it's not like I have a lot of dating experience,

329
23:39.898 --> 23:41.150
so I'm kind of clueless.

330
23:46.238 --> 23:47.698
I was pretty drunk that day too.

331
23:49.950 --> 23:51.493
You know, that...

332
23:52.828 --> 23:53.829
That...

333
23:56.915 --> 23:58.375
That day...

334
24:00.210 --> 24:01.211
when you...

335
24:03.672 --> 24:05.924
That day? What do you mean by "that day"?

336
24:08.594 --> 24:09.595
That...

337
24:11.055 --> 24:15.017
Do you mean the day of my welcome party?

338
24:15.601 --> 24:16.602
Yes.

339
24:18.562 --> 24:20.397
Did I throw up on your clothes?

340
24:20.481 --> 24:21.482
Hmm?

341
24:22.483 --> 24:23.776
No, not that.

342
24:25.527 --> 24:26.528
[sighs wearily]

343
24:26.612 --> 24:30.199
Well, I remember I was singing. No, actually...

344
24:30.866 --> 24:32.951
I remember getting into the taxi.

345
24:34.244 --> 24:36.163
But after that, I don't remember anything.

346
24:38.582 --> 24:41.502
You don't remember? Anything at all?

347
24:42.669 --> 24:46.090
Did I hit you or curse at you or something?

348
24:46.965 --> 24:48.133
No.

349
24:48.217 --> 24:49.551
And I didn't throw up either?

350
24:49.635 --> 24:50.761
No, you didn't.

351
24:54.515 --> 24:56.809
[sighing] I don't remember what I did,

352
24:57.726 --> 25:01.522
but if I did something wrong, I'm so sorry.

353
25:02.856 --> 25:05.317
I didn't mean to do it, I was just...

354
25:06.110 --> 25:07.820
I'm so sorry.

355
25:10.322 --> 25:13.117
It's okay. If you don't remember, don't worry about it.

356
25:14.451 --> 25:16.120
I can't handle alcohol very well.

357
25:16.203 --> 25:19.123
Whenever I drink, I always end up doing something stupid.

358
25:22.417 --> 25:23.418
I'm sorry.

359
25:24.002 --> 25:26.505
No. It was my bad.

360
25:27.339 --> 25:28.590
It's just... [sighs]

361
25:32.636 --> 25:33.637
Are you done eating?

362
25:35.389 --> 25:36.390
Yes.

363
25:36.473 --> 25:38.142
If you're done, should we head out?

364
25:53.907 --> 25:55.909
I'll walk you to the bus stop.

365
25:58.745 --> 26:02.499
By the way, when will I get my computer?

366
26:04.209 --> 26:06.336
That? You'll get it soon.

367
26:07.504 --> 26:08.755
When exactly is "soon"?

368
26:10.757 --> 26:11.758
[sighing]

369
26:12.968 --> 26:15.679
They've shipped it, so it should be here in a few days.

370
26:16.972 --> 26:20.684
How many days exactly? Tomorrow? The day after?

371
26:21.685 --> 26:24.146
How am I supposed to know exactly?

372
26:26.148 --> 26:29.359
So you don't know when it'll get here.

373
26:30.611 --> 26:33.322
What am I supposed to do until then? Just sit around?

374
26:34.781 --> 26:37.618
Well, like I said earlier, you can read papers and study.

375
26:38.869 --> 26:41.246
I can read papers at home too.

376
26:41.330 --> 26:43.498
What's the point of coming to the lab, then?

377
26:46.084 --> 26:47.085
Jeez.

378
26:49.046 --> 26:54.092
And if there's only one computer, you should've given it to me first.

379
26:54.718 --> 26:57.763
Why did you give it to Kim Sejin? He joined after me. I have seniority.

380
26:57.846 --> 26:58.847
[Minjae sighs]

381
27:00.724 --> 27:01.725
Hey, you...

382
27:02.309 --> 27:04.436
You don't have seniority.

383
27:04.519 --> 27:06.772
You joined us just three days before he did.

384
27:07.272 --> 27:09.775
I don't care if it was three days or four days.

385
27:09.858 --> 27:12.444
You still should've given it to me first, not him.

386
27:14.279 --> 27:16.073
Why do you think I gave it to him?

387
27:16.573 --> 27:19.284
You need MATLAB to run Simulink,

388
27:19.368 --> 27:21.620
and that computer already has it installed.

389
27:21.703 --> 27:23.622
That's why I gave it to him.

390
27:24.414 --> 27:25.874
And frankly, you...

391
27:25.958 --> 27:29.294
Do you even know how to use MATLAB? What about Simulink?

392
27:32.547 --> 27:33.715
If I don't know...

393
27:34.633 --> 27:37.260
Then you can teach me, right?

394
27:37.344 --> 27:40.138
Don't look down on me, and show me. I'm a fast learner.

395
27:40.222 --> 27:42.474
When did I look down on you?

396
27:43.433 --> 27:44.601
What are you, a high schooler?

397
27:44.685 --> 27:46.269
-An undergrad? -[sighs]

398
27:46.353 --> 27:49.523
Seriously, do I have to teach you every little thing?

399
27:50.565 --> 27:53.735
You need to look things up and study on your own. And I...

400
27:54.486 --> 27:57.572
I even told you to read papers. But you called it sitting around.

401
27:58.532 --> 28:01.284
Fine. If reading papers is just sitting around,

402
28:01.368 --> 28:02.953
go home and sit around.

403
28:03.036 --> 28:04.246
Don't come into the lab.

404
28:11.294 --> 28:12.921
Do you have anything else to say?

405
28:16.675 --> 28:20.595
I know you never liked me from the start.

406
28:22.222 --> 28:24.307
You didn't even want me to switch majors.

407
28:27.519 --> 28:29.396
I'll just take the subway home today.

408
28:29.980 --> 28:30.981
[grunts]

409
28:34.901 --> 28:37.112
[muttering softly] God. You've got to be kidding me.

410
28:39.948 --> 28:42.951
[♪ melancholic music playing]

411
28:49.374 --> 28:52.252
♪ Unless this first time is ♪

412
28:52.335 --> 28:54.713
♪ Also the last time ♪

413
28:55.297 --> 28:57.215
♪ There'll be a next time ♪

414
28:57.299 --> 28:59.843
♪ And maybe we can try again ♪

415
29:02.471 --> 29:05.348
♪ You threw me a life line ♪

416
29:05.432 --> 29:07.350
♪ You were kind enough ♪

417
29:07.434 --> 29:10.103
♪ To open what was shut ♪

418
29:10.687 --> 29:13.106
♪ But then I shut it again ♪

419
29:14.524 --> 29:17.652
♪ We got off on a bad start ♪

420
29:22.616 --> 29:27.245
♪ You don't know the half of my heart ♪

421
29:29.164 --> 29:31.958
♪ It pours like rain ♪

422
29:33.168 --> 29:35.712
♪ You don't know ♪

423
29:35.796 --> 29:39.341
♪ The half of my pain ♪

424
29:47.140 --> 29:48.975
♪ When I was young ♪

425
29:49.434 --> 29:51.603
♪ I grew up a little too fast ♪

426
29:52.562 --> 29:55.065
♪ I was wearing a child's mask ♪

427
29:55.148 --> 29:58.401
♪ But I saw the worst of it ♪

428
29:59.694 --> 30:01.196
♪ And then here you come ♪

429
30:01.279 --> 30:05.325
♪ Like stardust falling from the sky ♪

430
30:05.408 --> 30:08.120
♪ Excuse me if I shield my eyes ♪

431
30:08.578 --> 30:13.792
♪ I don't want to get hurt from it ♪

432
30:14.668 --> 30:18.380
♪ We got off on a bad start ♪

433
30:22.509 --> 30:24.386
♪ You don't know ♪

434
30:25.220 --> 30:27.639
♪ The half of my heart ♪

435
30:28.890 --> 30:31.893
♪ It pours like rain ♪

436
30:33.145 --> 30:35.147
♪ You don't know ♪

437
30:35.689 --> 30:41.236
♪ The half of my pain ♪

438
30:57.335 --> 31:01.047
♪ Oh, it's a shame, I know ♪

439
31:08.138 --> 31:12.142
♪ My mind says "stop" ♪

440
31:13.143 --> 31:15.937
♪ When my heart says "go" ♪

441
31:16.021 --> 31:17.564
SEOHAN NATIONAL UNIVERSITY TEST PAPER NAME KIM SEJIN

442
31:27.449 --> 31:30.368
SEOHAN NATIONAL UNIVERSITY TEST PAPER NAME LIM YOUJIN

443
31:30.452 --> 31:33.955
♪ We got off on a bad start ♪

444
31:38.418 --> 31:40.337
♪ You don't know ♪

445
31:41.046 --> 31:43.006
♪ The half of my heart ♪

446
31:44.799 --> 31:47.886
♪ It pours like rain ♪

447
31:49.137 --> 31:51.181
♪ You don't know ♪

448
31:51.264 --> 31:56.102
♪ The half of my pain ♪

449
32:06.321 --> 32:07.322
[♪ music ends]

450
32:20.502 --> 32:21.670
[inhales]

451
32:24.339 --> 32:25.340
[sighs]

452
32:28.009 --> 32:29.469
All right, let's see.

453
32:44.776 --> 32:45.860
Let's see.

454
32:49.322 --> 32:50.490
[phone clicks]

455
32:52.075 --> 32:53.493
[line ringing]

456
32:53.576 --> 32:54.577
Hello?

457
32:55.704 --> 32:58.873
You picked up fast. Hey, I have something to ask you.

458
33:00.625 --> 33:04.212
What do you mean, birthday? Please. Why don't you worry about your boyfriend?

459
33:06.840 --> 33:11.678
Anyway, that's not why I called. That computer you used, what brand was it?

460
33:14.431 --> 33:19.394
Yeah. You know, the one you used in the lab. That one.

461
33:24.983 --> 33:26.109
[phone vibrating]

462
33:32.657 --> 33:34.075
PARK MINJAE

463
33:34.159 --> 33:36.077
[Minjae] You better show up on time tomorrow.

464
33:36.161 --> 33:39.039
If you're late, I'm going to send you to Dieland.

465
33:39.122 --> 33:41.124
[♪ theme music playing]

466
34:57.659 --> 34:58.660
Hi.

467
35:01.663 --> 35:02.747
You aren't late.

468
35:03.748 --> 35:04.749
No.

469
35:07.585 --> 35:08.920
Did you have breakfast?

470
35:10.004 --> 35:12.006
[♪ fun music playing]

471
35:59.262 --> 36:01.097
Isn't that Lim Youjin?

472
36:02.307 --> 36:04.976
It's her, right? And next to her is the research assistant.

473
36:05.977 --> 36:09.689
She just fits in wherever she goes. She makes friends so easily too.

474
36:11.399 --> 36:12.525
It's nice to see.

475
36:14.235 --> 36:16.154
Do you happen to know him too?

476
36:17.947 --> 36:18.990
[chuckles awkwardly]

477
36:19.073 --> 36:20.784
I don't really know him.

478
36:37.091 --> 36:38.092
[beeps]

479
36:41.012 --> 36:43.598
Go on in. Come on.

480
36:53.608 --> 36:54.609
Oh!

481
36:55.109 --> 36:56.820
When did this get here?

482
36:57.946 --> 36:59.364
Well, I don't know.

483
37:00.406 --> 37:01.407
Oh.

484
37:01.491 --> 37:05.078
Was it delivered last night? It must've been last night, after we left.

485
37:05.161 --> 37:08.331
I told you it'd be here soon. I told you to just wait a little.

486
37:08.414 --> 37:10.667
Yeah, that was faster than I thought.

487
37:11.876 --> 37:13.503
Try turning it on. Here.

488
37:27.475 --> 37:28.476
[keyboard clacks]

489
37:33.523 --> 37:35.483
Wow, it's so fast. [gasps]

490
37:37.485 --> 37:39.445
All the software's already set up, too.

491
37:40.989 --> 37:43.241
This is brand-new. I got a brand-new computer.

492
37:43.324 --> 37:44.325
Yeah.

493
37:45.410 --> 37:46.494
Do you like it?

494
37:47.036 --> 37:49.122
Yeah. I absolutely love it.

495
37:50.373 --> 37:53.042
It's really expensive.

496
37:53.918 --> 37:57.755
Yeah, I can tell by just looking at it. This is an expensive, latest model.

497
37:58.590 --> 38:00.174
So the rumor was true.

498
38:00.800 --> 38:02.427
Rumor? What rumor?

499
38:02.969 --> 38:06.848
I heard engineering schools have money and get tons of corporate sponsorships.

500
38:06.931 --> 38:09.684
What? Engineering schools don't have a lot of money.

501
38:10.226 --> 38:13.313
Maybe you don't, but our school does.

502
38:14.772 --> 38:17.442
[sighs] Thank you, school, and whoever made this happen.

503
38:17.525 --> 38:19.068
I'll take good care of it.

504
38:25.074 --> 38:26.409
We got a new computer?

505
38:28.369 --> 38:30.288
Oh. When did you get it?

506
38:31.122 --> 38:32.373
It's the latest model.

507
38:32.457 --> 38:34.459
-Yeah. -This thing is high-end!

508
38:35.376 --> 38:38.087
What GPU does it have? I bet it's got a lot of storage too.

509
38:38.212 --> 38:39.213
Uh...

510
38:39.923 --> 38:42.508
[sighing grimly] My computer was so slow

511
38:42.592 --> 38:45.678
trying to run MATLAB, SolidWorks, and RecurDyn all at once.

512
38:45.762 --> 38:47.430
-Yeah. -This is perfect.

513
38:48.473 --> 38:49.474
Huh?

514
38:49.557 --> 38:50.558
I can...

515
38:52.352 --> 38:53.561
use this, right?

516
38:59.067 --> 39:00.193
[sighs softly]

517
39:01.486 --> 39:05.615
I... can use this, right?

518
39:08.660 --> 39:09.661
This?

519
39:15.625 --> 39:18.753
Right, but then...

520
39:19.379 --> 39:21.255
Yeah, I mean, you...

521
39:22.840 --> 39:26.636
You'll probably get more use out of it.

522
39:28.137 --> 39:34.352
Then, Youjin, you take that one, and Sejin, you take this one.

523
39:34.435 --> 39:35.436
Yes!

524
39:38.064 --> 39:39.232
What's wrong?

525
39:41.192 --> 39:42.193
What are you doing?

526
39:43.736 --> 39:45.947
I said, what are you doing?

527
39:46.656 --> 39:48.366
I can't take this anymore.

528
39:49.659 --> 39:52.078
Take what? You can just use any computer.

529
39:52.161 --> 39:53.496
-They're the same. -Forget it.

530
39:53.579 --> 39:55.206
I don't need any of this anymore.

531
39:55.289 --> 39:57.458
I clearly don't have what it takes. I'm useless.

532
39:57.542 --> 39:59.877
I was never qualified to be here in the first place.

533
40:00.670 --> 40:03.089
Sticking around when lack the qualifications or skills

534
40:03.172 --> 40:05.299
would only make things harder for everyone.

535
40:06.384 --> 40:08.344
I just can't do this anymore.

536
40:09.303 --> 40:10.596
I'm leaving the lab.

537
40:11.431 --> 40:12.432
What?

538
40:12.932 --> 40:16.352
I stay up studying every night and only get three, four hours of sleep.

539
40:16.978 --> 40:18.604
I'm reading papers and trying hard.

540
40:18.688 --> 40:22.525
But no matter how hard I try, I just realize how much I don't know.

541
40:23.818 --> 40:26.988
No, it's more than that. The amount I don't know keeps growing.

542
40:27.071 --> 40:29.615
The more I read, the more I realize I don't know.

543
40:30.158 --> 40:33.870
So what am I supposed to do? What more do you want from me?

544
40:37.540 --> 40:40.585
I already told you it was going to be hard

545
40:42.378 --> 40:44.881
and to think carefully before you make a decision.

546
40:48.009 --> 40:49.010
Fine.

547
40:49.969 --> 40:51.387
I guess it's my fault again.

548
40:54.223 --> 40:55.767
Thanks for the lesson.

549
40:59.854 --> 41:00.855
All right.

550
41:02.023 --> 41:04.859
Bring me your withdrawal form and a written explanation by tomorrow.

551
41:04.942 --> 41:06.110
I'll email them to you.

552
41:17.455 --> 41:18.706
What's going on?

553
41:18.790 --> 41:20.875
Minjae, did something happen?

554
41:32.470 --> 41:33.471
What's the matter?

555
41:34.388 --> 41:35.515
Did something happen?

556
41:36.015 --> 41:37.100
I'm not sure.

557
42:03.000 --> 42:05.002
[♪ pensive music playing]

558
42:24.105 --> 42:25.481
[sighs]

559
42:40.204 --> 42:42.206
[muffled sobs]

560
42:48.004 --> 42:50.006
[sobbing]

561
42:56.137 --> 42:57.138
[sighs]

562
43:02.768 --> 43:07.273
SEOHAN NATIONAL UNIVERSITY TEST PAPER NAME LIM YOUJIN

563
43:07.356 --> 43:11.736
SEOHAN NATIONAL UNIVERSITY TEST PAPER NAME KIM SEJIN

564
43:12.320 --> 43:15.489
Come on, you did a pretty good job. Why are you crying?

565
43:16.199 --> 43:18.784
[crying] What do you mean, pretty good? It's a mess.

566
43:23.539 --> 43:28.085
I made the question too hard. Yeah, I...

567
43:28.169 --> 43:32.131
What about Kim Sejin? How did Kim Sejin do so well?

568
43:33.090 --> 43:34.592
Is he a genius?

569
43:34.675 --> 43:36.677
Is he a genius and I'm just stupid?

570
43:37.178 --> 43:41.474
Hey, He's him and you're you. Why compare yourself to him?

571
43:41.557 --> 43:44.810
I'm not comparing myself to him. I'm just so stupid.

572
43:46.062 --> 43:47.897
Maybe you're a genius.

573
43:48.606 --> 43:50.358
Are you making fun of me right now?

574
43:53.611 --> 43:55.780
At the beginning of the movie Good Will Hunting,

575
43:56.447 --> 43:59.450
Matt Damon's character works as a janitor at MIT. But then--

576
43:59.533 --> 44:01.744
I told you I haven't seen that movie.

577
44:01.827 --> 44:03.746
Kim Sejin has, but I haven't.

578
44:03.829 --> 44:07.833
So go talk about that movie with Kim Sejin and leave me alone.

579
44:09.585 --> 44:11.671
Why did you even let me in?

580
44:12.213 --> 44:15.508
I haven't seen the movie, I can't do math, and I'm so stupid.

581
44:15.591 --> 44:16.842
[sobbing]

582
44:18.511 --> 44:21.931
[sniffles] Forget it. Let's just stop here.

583
44:23.140 --> 44:26.310
I don't want to keep going on and on like this either.

584
44:29.230 --> 44:32.942
I'm so sorry for causing you so much trouble all this time.

585
44:34.819 --> 44:39.824
I may be leaving, but I'll keep rooting for you from afar.

586
44:41.158 --> 44:43.744
No. Hey, wait. Okay, fine.

587
44:43.828 --> 44:46.580
Okay, sit down for a second. Hey, just for a second.

588
44:54.005 --> 44:55.631
Then, have you seen Harry Potter?

589
44:58.134 --> 45:01.178
Come on, you've seen that one, right?

590
45:01.262 --> 45:02.346
[♪ comical music playing]

591
45:02.430 --> 45:04.640
In Harry Potter, there's this talking hat.

592
45:04.724 --> 45:08.102
When Harry Potter puts it on, it tells him,

593
45:08.185 --> 45:12.898
"You're a Gryffindor. You're a Gryffindor."

594
45:14.608 --> 45:16.152
We have one at our school too.

595
45:17.570 --> 45:18.863
A talking hat.

596
45:20.072 --> 45:21.240
Want to meet it?

597
45:26.245 --> 45:27.580
Okay. Come this way.

598
45:31.500 --> 45:32.501
Oh?

599
45:34.211 --> 45:35.796
I guess he hasn't come in yet.

600
45:35.880 --> 45:37.923
[footsteps approaching]

601
45:40.801 --> 45:42.345
Oh!

602
45:42.428 --> 45:45.097
-Good morning, Professor. -Hi.

603
45:45.181 --> 45:47.058
Do you have a minute?

604
45:48.267 --> 45:49.518
Sure. Yeah, come in.

605
45:59.111 --> 46:00.821
[whispering] Is he the talking hat?

606
46:02.114 --> 46:03.616
[whispering] Yeah, he is.

607
46:11.791 --> 46:14.585
Sorry, my assistant is not here yet. Is this okay?

608
46:14.668 --> 46:17.004
-Yes, it's okay. Thank you. -Please, sit down.

609
46:17.088 --> 46:18.089
Thank you.

610
46:19.215 --> 46:20.883
So you want me to look at something?

611
46:21.384 --> 46:23.552
Right. It's just this...

612
46:26.138 --> 46:27.139
Here.

613
46:31.018 --> 46:32.019
Didn't...

614
46:33.479 --> 46:34.772
I look at this the other day?

615
46:34.855 --> 46:37.358
Yes, that's right. You looked it over last time

616
46:37.441 --> 46:40.319
and said it showed signs of genius.

617
46:40.403 --> 46:41.404
I did?

618
46:41.487 --> 46:42.488
Yes.

619
46:45.408 --> 46:47.952
I said I saw potential, not signs of genius.

620
46:50.788 --> 46:51.789
Ah.

621
46:51.872 --> 46:54.083
Is she the one who's from a different department?

622
46:54.166 --> 46:55.960
Yes, that's right. It's her.

623
46:58.921 --> 47:00.673
Have we met before?

624
47:01.257 --> 47:02.258
Sorry?

625
47:03.050 --> 47:04.510
I feel like we've met somewhere.

626
47:07.012 --> 47:09.265
I don't think we've met.

627
47:10.516 --> 47:11.517
Okay.

628
47:13.352 --> 47:16.647
Last time, you said she had talent--

629
47:16.730 --> 47:17.731
Yeah.

630
47:21.652 --> 47:22.903
Let me ask you one thing.

631
47:23.571 --> 47:26.157
This is a basic question.

632
47:27.158 --> 47:28.784
Why does one plus one equal two?

633
47:30.870 --> 47:32.246
[Minjae] Mmm...

634
47:33.789 --> 47:35.666
Because it conventionally represents--

635
47:35.749 --> 47:38.002
So why was the numeral 2 chosen to represent it?

636
47:40.713 --> 47:42.673
Because it looks pretty?

637
47:44.091 --> 47:45.801
See? She thinks differently.

638
47:46.385 --> 47:47.386
Oh.

639
47:48.471 --> 47:49.763
[chuckles awkwardly]

640
47:49.847 --> 47:51.348
Don't you think it's pretty?

641
47:51.432 --> 47:54.101
I think about that a lot when I'm solving math problems.

642
47:54.894 --> 47:57.646
You know, the harmony, the way things change...

643
47:57.730 --> 48:00.816
Sometimes it feels like a dance, or even a song.

644
48:01.233 --> 48:02.401
Hmm.

645
48:03.152 --> 48:04.278
Hmm.

646
48:04.361 --> 48:05.446
That's romantic.

647
48:06.363 --> 48:07.364
Pardon?

648
48:07.448 --> 48:13.787
Yeah, I think I heard somewhere that math is the language of God.

649
48:13.871 --> 48:15.956
Right. That's romantic too.

650
48:16.582 --> 48:19.793
That it's the language of God translated into human language.

651
48:19.877 --> 48:20.878
-Right. -Yeah.

652
48:23.714 --> 48:27.009
If numbers are God's language,

653
48:27.635 --> 48:31.639
then this answer is God being pretty chatty.

654
48:32.389 --> 48:37.061
But when you're learning a new language, being chatty is actually a huge advantage.

655
48:40.606 --> 48:42.399
I wouldn't call it genius,

656
48:44.068 --> 48:46.695
but I do see talent and potential.

657
48:47.196 --> 48:48.197
That's how I'd put it.

658
48:52.076 --> 48:54.370
Are you interested in continuing your studies?

659
48:55.329 --> 48:56.330
Uh...

660
48:57.706 --> 48:58.791
Hmm...

661
48:59.416 --> 49:00.543
Mmm.

662
49:00.626 --> 49:03.087
Well, think about it.

663
49:03.921 --> 49:05.548
Okay, I'll think about it.

664
49:16.392 --> 49:19.603
That professor is a bit strange, isn't he?

665
49:22.106 --> 49:23.107
Yeah.

666
49:24.650 --> 49:27.027
Everyone says he's a genius, though.

667
49:29.655 --> 49:33.117
A lot of geniuses are weird, though. They're kind of nuts.

668
49:33.951 --> 49:37.955
Then you must be a super, super, super genius.

669
49:43.711 --> 49:47.965
Anyway, I knew I had talent. It just hasn't blossomed yet.

670
49:49.174 --> 49:50.718
I'm not like Kim Sejin.

671
49:51.468 --> 49:55.431
I'm a genius, and he's just a smart man.

672
49:59.018 --> 50:02.062
Then will you let him use the computer?

673
50:03.105 --> 50:05.441
Not just the computer. He can use whatever he wants.

674
50:06.150 --> 50:08.652
Now, I'm someone who speaks the language of God.

675
50:08.736 --> 50:10.362
[laughs]

676
50:10.446 --> 50:13.407
Which means I'm a goddess. A genius goddess.

677
50:15.117 --> 50:16.619
[both laugh]

678
50:16.702 --> 50:19.246
You're really... You're really cute.

679
50:26.712 --> 50:28.297
-Let's go. -Okay.

680
50:30.966 --> 50:32.301
Done with that? I'll take it.

681
50:33.093 --> 50:34.094
Thank you.

682
50:40.100 --> 50:43.312
[Seohyun] I'm asking why you were using Minjae's computer.

683
50:43.395 --> 50:44.980
I gave it to him for his birthday.

684
50:45.773 --> 50:47.358
-I thought it was school-- -Louder.

685
50:47.441 --> 50:48.442
-Hey! -You thought it--

686
50:48.525 --> 50:49.985
What the... When did you get here?

687
50:50.069 --> 50:51.695
What? I just got here. Why?

688
50:52.321 --> 50:54.156
Didn't you go to work today?

689
50:54.239 --> 50:55.574
I took the afternoon off.

690
50:55.658 --> 50:58.827
Hey, will you please keep the kids in line?

691
50:58.911 --> 51:01.205
There's no discipline around here. Absolutely none.

692
51:01.288 --> 51:02.289
[sighs]

693
51:02.956 --> 51:05.542
I got busy at work and stopped checking in for a while,

694
51:05.626 --> 51:08.379
and this is what happens to the lab?

695
51:08.962 --> 51:11.423
Nobody even knew it's your birthday today.

696
51:11.507 --> 51:12.591
-Hey. -Well...

697
51:12.675 --> 51:15.969
Minjae goes by the lunar calendar for his birthday, and I got mixed up.

698
51:16.053 --> 51:18.472
If you got them mixed up, just celebrate both!

699
51:19.056 --> 51:20.265
How hard is that?

700
51:20.808 --> 51:22.142
No, it's not hard.

701
51:23.560 --> 51:26.980
You've gotten way too comfortable. You have no respect for Minjae, do you?

702
51:27.064 --> 51:28.232
[all] No.

703
51:28.774 --> 51:30.192
[yells] Everybody, out!

704
51:30.693 --> 51:31.694
What are you doing?

705
51:31.777 --> 51:33.028
[♪ theme song playing]

706
51:33.112 --> 51:34.697
Too slow!

707
51:38.992 --> 51:40.160
Aren't you going to go?

708
51:40.786 --> 51:41.787
Me too?

709
51:41.870 --> 51:44.248
Of course. Do you think you're an exception?

710
51:45.124 --> 51:46.250
-No. -Uh...

711
51:49.878 --> 51:51.630
What? What is it?

712
52:12.985 --> 52:15.612
[whispering] Where are we going now?

713
52:16.363 --> 52:18.907
[whispering] We're driving to Dieland.

714
52:18.991 --> 52:20.075
[gasps]

715
52:20.159 --> 52:24.079
Wait, Dieland is real? It actually exists?

716
52:26.874 --> 52:29.126
[whispering] By the way, why is she in a school uniform?

717
52:31.628 --> 52:35.966
[softly] Most engineering students are nuts.

718
52:39.511 --> 52:41.638
[whispering] It's not about being engineering students.

719
52:41.722 --> 52:44.141
I think it's a Seohan National University thing.

720
52:44.224 --> 52:46.727
KAIST wasn't like this. Everyone there was normal.

721
52:46.810 --> 52:50.105
Jeez, you're wearing a school uniform. You've got to be kidding me.

722
52:50.606 --> 52:53.567
What? This is what you're supposed to wear to a birthday party.

723
52:53.650 --> 52:54.651
[sighs]

724
52:54.735 --> 52:56.403
I told you to wear yours too.

725
52:57.613 --> 52:59.364
Hey, that still fits you?

726
53:00.449 --> 53:03.535
I know, right? I'm still fit. I can totally pull it off.

727
53:03.619 --> 53:05.788
I've gained weight, so mine doesn't fit anymore.

728
53:06.705 --> 53:07.915
Let's get you a new one.

729
53:08.582 --> 53:09.583
No.

730
53:10.334 --> 53:12.586
Then we can match every year on your birthday.

731
53:12.669 --> 53:13.796
I don't need it.

732
53:14.338 --> 53:16.507
-Should I get you one? -I said, I don't need it.

733
53:16.590 --> 53:17.716
Why not?

734
53:17.800 --> 53:19.510
-I'll buy a new one. -I don't want it.

735
53:19.593 --> 53:21.762
I'm never going to wear it. No way.

736
53:37.402 --> 53:40.948
I haven't been here in ages. But why is this place called Dieland?

737
53:42.449 --> 53:45.452
[screaming]

738
54:22.781 --> 54:25.534
[screaming]

739
54:43.385 --> 54:44.761
[Sejin] I didn't realize it before,

740
54:46.179 --> 54:48.140
but are those two a couple?

741
54:49.474 --> 54:52.728
She got him an expensive computer for his birthday,

742
54:53.270 --> 54:54.646
and they seem really close.

743
54:55.188 --> 54:57.858
They're not a couple, but they're high school sweethearts.

744
54:57.941 --> 55:01.695
No. It wasn't mutual, it was a crush.

745
55:02.529 --> 55:04.156
It was just a one-sided crush.

746
55:06.658 --> 55:10.871
Who had a crush on who? Did Seohyun have a crush on Minjae?

747
55:10.954 --> 55:13.540
No, it's not like that.

748
55:15.417 --> 55:19.212
In high school, Seohyun was the top student

749
55:19.296 --> 55:23.592
and the most popular girl in the school, while Minjae was dead last.

750
55:23.675 --> 55:28.555
But he studied really hard to get into the same university as her.

751
55:28.639 --> 55:30.140
That's how he got into our school

752
55:30.223 --> 55:32.476
and even followed her into mechanical engineering.

753
55:33.644 --> 55:35.604
[Chansoo] It's straight out of a coming-of-age manga.

754
55:36.313 --> 55:38.273
And a high school romance.

755
55:38.982 --> 55:42.444
It's kind of like Slam Dunk. Haruko Akagi and Hanamichi Sakuragi.

756
55:43.570 --> 55:46.156
But they never dated? Why not?

757
55:46.239 --> 55:49.951
Because Seohyun was super popular, while Minjae was the kind of guy

758
55:50.035 --> 55:53.372
who second-guessed everything and made things way too complicated.

759
55:54.873 --> 55:56.208
That's why they never got together.

760
55:59.044 --> 56:00.671
Well, maybe that's not the reason.

761
56:02.964 --> 56:04.591
Maybe it was because of his leg.

762
56:07.803 --> 56:09.179
-Just try it on once. -No.

763
56:09.262 --> 56:10.347
Please.

764
56:10.430 --> 56:12.224
-Damn it. -Here. Just take this.

765
56:12.307 --> 56:14.017
Hey, guys, take one each. [grunts]

766
56:18.480 --> 56:20.190
Seohyun, when are we going home?

767
56:20.273 --> 56:23.568
We should stay for the parade and the fireworks. That's the highlight.

768
56:23.652 --> 56:27.239
Wait, then we'll have to stay here past eight.

769
56:27.781 --> 56:29.157
[laughs mischievously]

770
56:29.241 --> 56:30.617
Your expressions...

771
56:30.701 --> 56:32.619
Look at you, Taeho, all grown up, huh?

772
56:32.703 --> 56:34.621
No, we're good. We don't need to see that.

773
56:34.705 --> 56:36.289
We're not kids. Come on, let's go.

774
56:36.373 --> 56:37.916
[Seohyun] Come on, that's the best part.

775
56:37.999 --> 56:40.210
-[Minjae] No, it's not. -[Seohyun] Come on, let's watch it.

776
56:40.293 --> 56:42.295
[♪ lively music playing]

777
57:06.278 --> 57:07.946
I read Slam Dunk.

778
57:09.489 --> 57:10.657
You read it?

779
57:13.702 --> 57:17.873
Hanamichi Sakuragi was bad at basketball, but he finds out Haruko likes it

780
57:17.956 --> 57:19.541
and he joins the basketball team.

781
57:19.624 --> 57:22.002
-That's basically it, right? -Yeah, you read it.

782
57:22.586 --> 57:23.587
It's fun, isn't it?

783
57:24.880 --> 57:26.173
Not to me.

784
57:27.174 --> 57:30.302
I guess you like stories like that? Because you relate to it so much?

785
57:31.303 --> 57:32.304
What?

786
57:35.390 --> 57:38.518
Sorry. I'm in a bit of a mood today.

787
57:40.729 --> 57:41.855
Why are you in a mood?

788
57:43.899 --> 57:45.484
I don't want to tell you why.

789
57:46.359 --> 57:49.237
It sounds childish and unreasonable, even to me.

790
57:52.741 --> 57:53.742
Unless...

791
57:58.288 --> 58:01.333
If you put this on and take a selfie with me,

792
58:01.416 --> 58:02.626
I think I'd feel better.

793
58:03.251 --> 58:04.252
No.

794
58:06.338 --> 58:08.298
Please, just one picture with it on.

795
58:08.381 --> 58:10.383
Why are you doing this? No, I don't want to.

796
58:10.967 --> 58:13.053
-Please, just once. -No.

797
58:13.136 --> 58:14.721
Not even once?

798
58:14.805 --> 58:18.809
Of course not. Why would you put that on your head? I don't get it. No.

799
58:19.768 --> 58:21.102
I won't wait long.

800
58:21.186 --> 58:22.562
[♪ slow pleasant music playing]

801
58:22.646 --> 58:23.730
Five.

802
58:25.440 --> 58:26.441
Four.

803
58:27.984 --> 58:28.985
Three.

804
58:30.278 --> 58:31.279
Two.

805
58:33.615 --> 58:34.616
One.

806
58:43.625 --> 58:46.711
But no pictures, okay? I'll put it on, and that's it.

807
58:55.387 --> 58:57.389
[♪ music builds up]

808
59:01.309 --> 59:03.311
[crowd cheering]

809
59:07.148 --> 59:10.819
♪ I can't say ♪

810
59:11.444 --> 59:14.739
♪ How long I've waited for you ♪

811
59:14.823 --> 59:18.660
♪ And I don't know ♪

812
59:19.160 --> 59:22.247
♪ How long I'll be with you ♪

813
59:23.540 --> 59:28.920
♪ Maybe I'm just a fool in love ♪

814
59:29.004 --> 59:35.010
♪ But still I wanna thank the stars above ♪

815
59:36.678 --> 59:41.474
♪ You're my home ♪

816
59:42.142 --> 59:48.773
♪ Too many years I've passed alone ♪

817
59:49.900 --> 59:53.945
♪ And now I'm home at last ♪

818
01:00:01.620 --> 01:00:04.289
♪ Meet me there ♪

819
01:00:05.206 --> 01:00:08.960
♪ Where all my cares are not around me ♪

820
01:00:09.044 --> 01:00:12.589
♪ It's anywhere ♪

821
01:00:12.672 --> 01:00:16.343
♪ That you're standing next to me ♪

822
01:00:17.218 --> 01:00:20.639
♪ A sacred place only we can go ♪

823
01:00:20.722 --> 01:00:22.474
Are you looking for anything specific?

824
01:00:24.517 --> 01:00:25.518
No.

825
01:00:25.602 --> 01:00:30.690
♪ A secret only you can know ♪

826
01:00:30.774 --> 01:00:33.860
♪ You're my home... ♪

827
01:00:33.944 --> 01:00:35.654
Would you like to take a closer look?

828
01:00:36.905 --> 01:00:38.323
No, I'm okay.

829
01:00:41.910 --> 01:00:45.622
Then could you show me this one?

830
01:00:45.705 --> 01:00:46.706
Sure.

831
01:00:50.085 --> 01:00:51.294
[phone vibrating]

832
01:00:53.505 --> 01:00:58.051
INCOMING CALL SUBIN

833
01:01:02.931 --> 01:01:04.933
[♪ music ends]

834
01:01:05.016 --> 01:01:06.017
[indistinct chatter]

835
01:01:09.145 --> 01:01:11.147
[♪ chill music playing on speakers]

836
01:01:27.580 --> 01:01:28.581
[Youjin sighs]

837
01:01:32.711 --> 01:01:34.546
It's been ages, hasn't it?

838
01:01:35.046 --> 01:01:36.256
Yeah.

839
01:01:36.339 --> 01:01:37.924
How have you been?

840
01:01:40.176 --> 01:01:43.304
It must be so hectic studying and working as a TA at the same time.

841
01:01:46.349 --> 01:01:47.934
I'm sorry. It's all because of me.

842
01:01:48.435 --> 01:01:49.436
Hmm?

843
01:01:51.604 --> 01:01:52.939
It's not because of you.

844
01:01:54.107 --> 01:01:56.651
I was never good at making clothes anyway.

845
01:01:57.444 --> 01:02:00.905
And I wasn't sure about joining Professor Kang's lab. You know that.

846
01:02:02.574 --> 01:02:06.077
Actually, I saw you on campus a few times.

847
01:02:07.120 --> 01:02:10.498
But I couldn't bring myself to say hi or act like I knew you.

848
01:02:13.960 --> 01:02:17.088
Well, that's... I know how small this field is.

849
01:02:19.007 --> 01:02:20.633
And you're still in the program.

850
01:02:21.217 --> 01:02:23.511
You have to study and get your degree,

851
01:02:23.595 --> 01:02:26.556
so, of course, you've got to stay on Professor Kang's good side.

852
01:02:28.600 --> 01:02:31.436
I'm the one who talked back to her and caused all that trouble.

853
01:02:32.062 --> 01:02:33.438
I was the one in the wrong.

854
01:02:34.856 --> 01:02:39.235
Actually, Professor Kang has cooled off quite a bit.

855
01:02:41.404 --> 01:02:45.784
She said if you apologized, she'd forgive you and accept it.

856
01:02:49.162 --> 01:02:50.747
She'd forgive me and accept it?

857
01:02:53.208 --> 01:02:55.543
Forgive me for what and accept what?

858
01:02:56.044 --> 01:02:59.380
Well, maybe "forgive" isn't exactly the right word.

859
01:03:02.759 --> 01:03:05.512
But what good does it do to get on the professor's bad side?

860
01:03:10.475 --> 01:03:12.519
Okay, I'll think about it.

861
01:03:12.602 --> 01:03:13.686
Really?

862
01:03:13.770 --> 01:03:14.771
Yeah.

863
01:03:18.817 --> 01:03:21.319
So, how's mechanical engineering? Are you enjoying it?

864
01:03:22.529 --> 01:03:23.822
Yeah, it's fun.

865
01:03:24.781 --> 01:03:27.492
The lab assistant is that guy from before, right?

866
01:03:29.327 --> 01:03:32.497
I honestly had no idea he was disabled.

867
01:03:33.581 --> 01:03:35.667
There was nothing unusual about the way he walked, right?

868
01:03:37.418 --> 01:03:39.420
He doesn't limp or anything.

869
01:03:41.005 --> 01:03:43.007
[♪ melancholic music playing]

870
01:03:50.515 --> 01:03:53.059
♪ Unless this first time is ♪

871
01:03:53.143 --> 01:03:56.312
♪ Also the last time ♪

872
01:03:56.396 --> 01:03:58.273
♪ There'll be a next time ♪

873
01:03:58.356 --> 01:04:00.817
♪ And maybe we can try again ♪

874
01:04:00.900 --> 01:04:03.486
[device beeping]

875
01:04:03.570 --> 01:04:06.406
♪ You threw me a life line ♪

876
01:04:06.489 --> 01:04:08.491
♪ You were kind enough ♪

877
01:04:08.575 --> 01:04:11.369
♪ To open what we shut ♪

878
01:04:11.452 --> 01:04:13.830
♪ But then I shut it again ♪

879
01:04:15.665 --> 01:04:19.127
♪ We got off on a bad start ♪

880
01:04:23.673 --> 01:04:25.425
♪ You don't know ♪

881
01:04:26.259 --> 01:04:29.012
♪ The half of my heart ♪

882
01:04:30.305 --> 01:04:33.600
♪ It pours like rain ♪

883
01:04:34.142 --> 01:04:36.769
♪ You don't know ♪

884
01:04:36.853 --> 01:04:40.273
♪ The half of my pain ♪

885
01:04:48.239 --> 01:04:50.408
♪ When I was young ♪

886
01:04:50.491 --> 01:04:53.286
♪ I grew up a little too fast ♪

887
01:04:53.369 --> 01:04:56.289
♪ I was wearing a child's mask ♪

888
01:04:56.372 --> 01:04:59.667
♪ But I saw the worst of it ♪

889
01:05:00.835 --> 01:05:02.670
♪ And then here you come ♪

890
01:05:02.754 --> 01:05:06.633
♪ Like stardust falling from the sky ♪

891
01:05:06.716 --> 01:05:09.344
♪ Excuse me if I shield my eyes ♪

892
01:05:09.427 --> 01:05:14.265
♪ I don't want to get hurt from it ♪

893
